{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774129314,"nonce":"Mf0PivnmW8ccKOw6A1VUTfhCTpA=","message":"**Updated architecture based on analysis round 2**\n\nKey corrections from Gemini critique and user feedback:\n\n1. **No new BackendType.** Channel connectivity is a capability flag on PTY backend (`channel_connected_at`), not a new `channel` type. Reduces blast radius.\n\n2. **Naming: PTY backend.** Not \"channel backend.\" Channels are also injected into SDK sessions.\n\n3. **Channel events UI: sub-tabs.** Channel-connected PTY sessions show Terminal | Events sub-tabs in the content area. Events tab has notification badge. Sidebar remains for parameters only.\n\n4. **Channel server discovery.** Must use absolute path to channel server script in --channels flag. This is a gap that needs concrete resolution.\n\n5. **SDK does NOT use user OAuth.** Confirmed: SDK requires ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, does not fall back to Claude Code subscription credentials. Two genuinely different auth paths.\n\n6. **Channels ARE bidirectional.** Channel servers can push `notifications/claude/channel` events into running sessions. This makes channel mode more capable than initially assessed — Mandible can proactively notify, not just provide tools.\n\n7. **Per-prompt parameter snapshots.** Not currently stored in SDK backend. New feature needed for message-level parameter visibility.","files":null}]}